BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[C3] SELF-DIRECTED LEARNING/LONGITUDINAL THEMES: Foundations Integ
 ratedCase: Obesity in the Real World Phase 1: Independent Study Modules (I
 SM)
DTSTART:20261005T160000Z
DTEND:20261005T175000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T051526Z
UID:f5278e21-4432-400f-b7c1-f3660445fb84_E198930@calendar.med.ualberta.ca
DESCRIPTION:Phase 1: Independent Study Modules (ISM)\nComplete these async
 hronous independent study modules hosted in Assess.med—designed with ded
 icated curricular time and space (Katz Small Group Rooms for Edmonton stud
 ents\, and HEC 204 for NAMP students)\, with the flexibility to engage out
 side of class during or after this dedicated time. These modules will be r
 eleased at 10 AM on Monday\, October 5\, and will remain open for you unti
 l 12 PM on Wednesday\, October 7. Completion is not mandatory\, they are n
 ot for marks\, and the modules will remain available for review after the 
 lecture for your ongoing learning (just like WOBEs). Each module features 
 video clips paired with formative\, open-book multiple-choice questions to
  test your understanding of biometrics\, weight bias frameworks\, and the 
 pathophysiology of obesity.\n\nPhase 2: Live 1-Hour Lecture\nParticipate i
 n this interactive\, live session on Wednesday\, October 7 at 1 PM\, where
  faculty will use the responses from the independent study modules to targ
 et high-yield teaching points that still meet the curricular objectives. T
 he session includes a debrief on high-yield topics\, a faculty role-play d
 emonstration on clinical communication\, a high-yield physiology deep-dive
 \, and Primary Care Network (PCN) team integration.\n\nWe have also includ
 ed the full lecture slide set for all 7 Modules in Cally for your referenc
 e!\nCourse: MED 511\n\nInstructors:\n	Roshan Abraham (jrabraha)\n	Shereen 
 Hamza (shamza)\n\nMy Group:\n	Name: TBL 16\n	Location: Katz 1078\n\nObject
 ives:\n	Describe how obesity is defined using BMI and waist circumference.
 \n	Examine how obesity is staged through the Edmonton Obesity Staging Syst
 em.\n	Describe common comorbid conditions that can occur with obesity.\n	D
 escribe initial lifestyle\, pharmacologic\, and surgical management of obe
 sity.\n	Participate in a patient-centred approach to discussing obesity wi
 th a patient.\n	Participate in communicating relevant concepts relating to
  metabolism to a patient with obesity using easy to understand language.\n
 	Practice engaging in shared decision making with a patient with obesity b
 y incorporating their unique context in management.\n	Describe how obesity
  is effectively managed by a multidisciplinary team.\n	Differentiate betwe
 en weight bias\, stigma\, and discrimination in clinical care.\n\nView thi
 s event online: https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198930
LOCATION:
URL:https://calendar.med.ualberta.ca/events/198930
END:VEVENT
